# Hostile images: one per finding, kept so it can never come back.
#
# Every row here was once a crash, a hang, a sanitizer report or a write from
# a read-only verb. The image is committed gzipped (a mostly-zero 4 MiB
# volume compresses to a few kilobytes) beside a JSON recipe saying which
# bytes were changed and why -- because "3 megabytes of bytes" is not a
# description of a bug, and a fixture nobody can explain is a fixture nobody
# will dare to change.
#
# Columns, whitespace-separated, one row per fixture:
#
#   file     the .img.gz, relative to this directory
#   mode     ro    only read verbs are run
#            rw    read verbs, then a write script and a structural check
#   verbs    comma-separated ext4dump verbs; a verb may carry its argument
#            with '+' standing in for the space (cat+/victim)
#   fix      the patch or commit that made it stop failing, or '-' if the
#            fixture is a known-open finding deliberately kept red
#   note     free text to the end of the line
#
# Every row asserts the same three things: exit code below 128 (no crash, no
# watchdog kill), no sanitizer line in the output, and the image byte-identical
# afterwards. A read verb that changes the medium is a finding whatever it
# returns.
#
# file                                mode  verbs                                    fix     note
0001-corrupt-extent-header.img.gz     ro    probe,ls+/,cat+/victim,extents+/victim,check  0048  eh_entries 0x4000 and eh_max 0xFFFF in the root header, which lives in the inode and so passed through no block validator
0002-inode-size-larger-than-the-block.img.gz  ro    probe,ls+/,check,df,groups  gate  s_inode_size 54915 with the superblock checksum re-stamped; the inode checksum routine then read 54915 bytes out of a block-sized buffer
0003-directory-past-its-extent-tree.img.gz  ro    probe,ls+/,check,orphans  0064  a directory whose i_size claims more blocks than its extent tree maps; the walk asserted on the hole and aborted
0004-inode-table-moved-under-an-xattr-walk.img.gz  ro    probe,ls+/,check,xattrwalk+/  0065  one byte in a group descriptor moves the inode table into the metadata region; the xattr walk then read past the inode buffer
0005-a-journal-that-replays-the-superblock.img.gz  rw    probe,ls+/,check  0066  a committed transaction staging arbitrary bytes for block 1, which is the superblock on a 1 KiB volume
0006-a-directory-entry-longer-than-its-block.img.gz  rw    probe,ls+/,check  0067  a directory entry whose rec_len runs past its block; the insert path asserted on it, and a rec_len of zero would have spun
0007-a-zero-length-directory-entry.img.gz  rw    probe,ls+/,check  0067  an entry whose rec_len is zero: the insert walk advanced by it and spun, holding the mount
0008-a-bitmap-marked-past-its-own-end.img.gz  ro    probe,ls+/,check,df,groups  0068  a BLOCK_UNINIT group whose head-block count exceeds its own bitmap; materialising it wrote past the block
0009-an-htree-count-past-its-limit.img.gz  ro    probe,walk+/,check  0069  an index block whose count exceeds its limit; the count sized the region the checksum read
0010-an-odd-group-descriptor-size.img.gz  ro    probe,ls+/,check,df  gate  s_desc_size odd, which lwext4 uses whether or not 64BIT is set; every descriptor pointer built from it was misaligned
0011-a-revision-0-superblock-with-an-inode-size-that-is-not-128.img.gz  ro    probe,ls+/,check  gate  fixture 0002 with s_rev_level set to 0: the gate used to substitute 128 for rev 0 instead of validating the field lwext4 actually reads
0012-a-directory-entry-at-the-last-byte-of-its-block.img.gz  ro    probe,ls+/d,cat+/d/z,check  0072  a directory entry one byte short of its block end; the linear lookup read its header past the buffer, bounded now by the header not the searched name
